      "sourceTextSha256": "8a83c49be55e081cdecb478a36622203cf553d94c07f02c9502c0fad38836e14",
      "text": "Day 6 · After breakfast, full-day excursion to the magnificent Perito Moreno Glacier, at the southwestern end of Lago Argentino, about 80 km from El Calafate. From the viewpoints and footbridges, admire its 60-metre-high ice front and watch enormous walls of ice break away and plunge into the waters of Brazo Rico or the Canal de los Témpanos (Ice Floes Channel).\n\nNamed after the explorer Francisco Pascasio Moreno, the glacier is one of the few in the region that is not retreating. Periodically it advances across the lake to the Magallanes Peninsula and blocks Brazo Rico; the water level then rises considerably until it carves through the ice and the barrier collapses in one of nature’s most spectacular displays.",
